  <static seed="1815" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionsCalculation/EquivalentFraction20.pg">
    <statement><p>Find an equivalent fraction to <m>\frac{2}{19}</m> with denominator <m>57</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{6}{57}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>From <m>2</m> to <m>6</m>, we multiplied by <m>6\div2=3</m>.</p>
<p>For a fraction, when we multiply the same number in both the numerator and denominator, the fraction<rsq/>s value doesn<rsq/>t change. We have:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{2}{19}=\frac{2\cdot3}{19\cdot3} = \frac{6}{57} }</m></p>
</solution>
